  "id": "shared-environment",
  "term": "shared environment",
  "definition": "Shared environment refers to influences that people in the same family or household have in common, which can make them more alike on a psychological ability or trait. In the source study, it describes common environmental factors that contributed to children’s emotion recognition and to the overlap between recognizing emotions from faces and from voices.",
